From: Tilo maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] btrfs: only verify the completed range of a large folio

end_folio_read() runs once per completed range of a folio, but
btrfs_verify_folio() handed the whole folio to fs-verity. With large
data folios, a folio can be filled by several bios, or by a bio plus
hole or inline handling. The first completion then hashes blocks that
are still under I/O (zeroed on allocation) and reports them as
corrupted, clears its own range's uptodate bit and makes the reader
retry the folio.

Verify only the range that completed. Merkle tree blocks are never
larger than the filesystem block size, and end_folio_read() ranges are
block aligned, so the range is always valid for fsverity_verify_blocks().

--- a/fs/btrfs/extent_io.c
+++ b/fs/btrfs/extent_io.c
@@ -504,7 +504,13 @@
 
 	if (!vi || btrfs_folio_test_uptodate(fs_info, folio, start, len))
 		return true;
-	return fsverity_verify_folio(vi, folio);
+	/*
+	 * Only [start, start + len) has finished reading.  The rest of a large
+	 * folio may still be under I/O from another bio, so verify just this
+	 * range.
+	 */
+	return fsverity_verify_blocks(vi, folio, len,
+				      offset_in_folio(folio, start));
 }
 
 static void end_folio_read(struct fsverity_info *vi, struct folio *folio,
